      en: "Tepe Maranjan is an archaeological mound in Balkh province, northern Afghanistan. The site dates from the Kushan Empire period and contains remains of a large urban settlement with a palace complex. Excavations in the 1960s uncovered houses, workshops, and an irrigation system. Finds include coins, pottery, and glassware. Tepe Maranjan provides insights into daily life in the Kushan period.",
